  "mixture": {
    "archetypes": 0.2,
    "neighbourhood": 0.6,
    "exploration": 0.2
  },
  "// archetypes": "Normalization runs once or twice per transformer block, on the same activation tensor the block's matmuls produce -- so its shapes are the model's hidden width against however many tokens are in flight, not arbitrary three-dimensional boxes.",
  "// neighbourhood": "hidden_dim is absent from the neighbourhood: it is fixed by the model architecture and takes a handful of values, so an interpolated 5000 is a width nobody ships. batch and seq_len are what actually vary between requests. hidden_dim moves among the widths shipped models use, as SDPA's head_dim does, rather than scaling to a width no model has."
}
